WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.140
Step right up, folks! We’ve got all kinds&nbsp;
of refreshing and tasty treats here for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.880
you today! Popcorn, peanuts, cotton&nbsp;
candy, and even fried dough! Yessiree,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:12.120
here at SCP Explained, we’re&nbsp;
offering the top-of-the-line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:15.960
anomalous delectable foodstuffs for all&nbsp;
of your circus-themed funtime occasions.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:21.780
And that’s because today - Yes! Today! On&nbsp;
this Youtube Platform! - Our infamous acronym&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:27.660
doesn’t stand for Secure Contain Protect:&nbsp;
it stands for Sweet Confectionary Products.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:32.820
And let me tell you, dear viewer, the SCP we’re&nbsp;
looking at today just might be the most decadent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:36.180
durable, and dangerous dessert&nbsp;
that’s ever desired to be devoured.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:42.960
We’re talking about SCP-3077, or as&nbsp;
they are better known, The Sugar Golems!

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.220
These little fellas are Safe class and&nbsp;
also totally harmless - so long as you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:50.100
take the proper precautions! What’s the matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.840
don’t ya believe me? Don’t you think it’s&nbsp;
nice of us to cover a safe SCP now and again?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.280
And hey now! Why all this dull talk about&nbsp;
rules and regulations in the first place?

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.680
You don’t go out to the carnival to not&nbsp;
take wild and exciting risks! Every spinny,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.520
twirly, and whirly ride on the fairgrounds&nbsp;
comes with a statistically higher chance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:13.620
of a tragic mishap befalling you and&nbsp;
any other thrill-seekers around you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:19.140
but we all take that chance anyway for&nbsp;
the extraordinary rush of the experience!

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:25.200
And such is the wacky and wonderful ways of&nbsp;
our adorable and questionably edible chums:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.820
The Sugar Golems! Don’t you just love ‘em,&nbsp;
folks? Ain’t they a sight for sore eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:35.460
and a pang for sweet teeth? Well, we’ve only&nbsp;
just gotten started! The best is yet to come,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:39.720
ladies and non-ladies! So pull up a chair&nbsp;
and be sure to watch what we’ve got in store!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:45.060
You can make like a piece of old candy and&nbsp;
“stick around!” Now that’s a knee-slapper,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:50.040
ain’t it? Sit back, relax and&nbsp;
make sure to enjoy the show!

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.540
You should also subscribe to SCP Explained if&nbsp;
you’d like to continue to be entertained. Hey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.500
that rhymed! Whaddaya know? I’m a poet,&nbsp;
and I didn’t even know it! How droll!

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.840
While SCP-3077 refers to the anomalous&nbsp;
substance contained in Site-81,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:07.680
the semi-humanoid instances,&nbsp;
which are nicknamed sugar golems,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.360
are themselves an animate and independent&nbsp;
by-product that naturally spawns from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:17.580
SCP-3077 whenever it is allowed to&nbsp;
exist outside of containment procedures.

00:02:17.580 --> 00:02:23.700
The most important of these containment procedures&nbsp;
being that SCP-3077 must remain at a constant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:29.580
temperature of well below its freezing point and&nbsp;
only be stored in containers full to capacity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:33.780
lest its aforementioned by-products&nbsp;
attempt to breach containment. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:40.620
total volume of SCP-3077 within the cryogenic&nbsp;
containment unit equals almost 2280 liters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:46.020
and it is believed to be the only known quantity&nbsp;
of the anomalous substance in existence.

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.180
For the sake of clarity in distinguishing&nbsp;
between SCP-3077 and its byproducts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:55.500
we’ll be referring to the main object&nbsp;
contained by the Foundation as SCP-3077,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:00.360
while the gooey little guys who we know to&nbsp;
spontaneously split off from the source of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:09.420
SCP-3077 will be regarded as SCP-3077-1. As&nbsp;
mentioned before, SCP-3077-1 instances have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:17.220
been affectionately dubbed The Sugar Golems. Every&nbsp;
instance of SCP-3077-1 resembles an approximately&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:24.540
one-meter tall gaunt humanoid composed of a pure&nbsp;
sugar-derived substance commonly known as treacle.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:28.800
And that’s molasses for all of y’all -&nbsp;
yeehaw! - cowboys over there in the U S of A!

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:33.720
If you’ve ever played the classic board game&nbsp;
Candyland, you’ll have some idea of what an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:39.840
individual instance of SCP-3077 looks like from&nbsp;
the beloved and often remembered character of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:45.540
Gloppy, who lives in the molasses swamp section&nbsp;
of the board and is also fittingly made out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:51.720
molasses himself. Yes, indeed, Gloppy is truly&nbsp;
a delight for a weary CandyLand player to meet.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:56.340
What did you say? Are you folks too young to know&nbsp;
about CandyLand? Well, that factoid certainly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.340 --> 00:04:01.380
makes this narrator feel pretty old. Then again,&nbsp;
I am taking on the mannerisms and attire of an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:06.300
old-fashioned carnival barker, so I suppose a&nbsp;
bit of novel antiquity comes with the territory.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:12.060
Regardless, the golems are each composed of&nbsp;
roughly 7 liters of sweet syrupy goodness,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:17.340
and very much like everyone's favorite character&nbsp;
Gloppy they all lack defined lower bodies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:22.980
can all emote through crude yet oddly endearing&nbsp;
vocalizations in the place of intelligible speech.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.980 --> 00:04:27.780
While their facial features are simplistic&nbsp;
and misshapen, the contours of concave eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:32.640
and a gaping mouth are usually present. The exact&nbsp;
number of these eyes and mouths is subject to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:38.640
variation, much like the color of the board spaces&nbsp;
in a wonderful wholesome family game of CandyLand.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:45.120
While every SCP-3077-1 instance is around the&nbsp;
same size, the body proportions and overall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:51.840
shape of each instance are rather fluid - pun&nbsp;
fully intended! Some possess oversized arms or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:57.780
bulbous heads, while others might be conjoined to&nbsp;
an adjacent sugar golem as if to show that the two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.780 --> 00:05:04.290
are as inseparable as a pair of best buddies. Or,&nbsp;
as some others might put it, a couple of B.F.F.F.s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.290 --> 00:05:10.080
- Best Friends for Fancy Frolicking. They&nbsp;
really are quite friendly-looking, aren’t they?

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:15.240
And aren’t they, they sure are! For the&nbsp;
only thing that these sugary sweet SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.240 --> 00:05:19.560
instances want is to be in the company&nbsp;
of human beings just like you. Yes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:24.300
you! Who else would I be talking to? It’s a hard&nbsp;
life for this worn-down carnie, let me tell ya!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:29.580
These little sugar golems love what they do and do&nbsp;
what they love, but that doesn’t mean that it's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.580 --> 00:05:35.940
time for fun and games! Even though SCP-3077-1&nbsp;
instances want to hang around human beings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:39.960
they don’t tend to stop at “hey” and “hello”&nbsp;
or whatever those appropriate greetings sound&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:44.880
like when they are being gurgled by a diminutive&nbsp;
molten sugar monster! Things can get out of hand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:50.100
real fast - just like an orange cream popsicle&nbsp;
melting in the sun of a late summer’s day!

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:54.540
Now listen up, it’s important that you&nbsp;
pay attention to what I say next! I’m&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:59.220
about to book-learn you about what to&nbsp;
do if an instance of SCP-3077-1 enters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:04.980
your personal space! The results of prolonged&nbsp;
contact with this SCP can end badly if you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:05.560
not careful, much like a certain dessert that&nbsp;
contains the words “by chocolate” and nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:09.720
good proceeding it! I’m not going to sugarcoat&nbsp;
any of the chewy details of your “gristly” fate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:13.440
and I promise you that it won’t be a&nbsp;
cakewalk, so don’t be a nerd and listen up!

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:18.540
Yes, that’s right, I called you a nerd. You know,&nbsp;
like nerds? The candy? How do you folks seriously&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:22.320
not know nerds? They were a classic Halloween&nbsp;
candy from the Wonka company and they were very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:26.880
popular back in the day! Oh? What’s that you&nbsp;
say? How long ago was back in the day for me?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:32.160
That’s a bit of a rude question, wouldn't&nbsp;
you say? Oooh…! Why I oughta…! Won’t you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:35.940
go ahead and knock it off with the wise guy&nbsp;
questions! What are you, a pack of smarties?

00:06:35.940 --> 00:06:40.680
Ha! I said Smarties! Get it?&nbsp;
It’s just like the—ah, nevermind.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:46.320
Let’s just move on to the explanation of how&nbsp;
to survive a close encounter with this SCP.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.020
That was the main reason you&nbsp;
came all the way to this here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.020 --> 00:06:52.800
educational and entertaining&nbsp;
video presentation, after all!

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:59.340
To pick up where I left off, instances&nbsp;
of SCP-3077-1 have a tendency to seek&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:06.060
out nearby human life. The reason for doing so is&nbsp;
surprisingly simple and alarmingly well… alarming!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.060 --> 00:07:12.060
These sticky saccharine simulacra are solely&nbsp;
set on slithering into people’s mouths for the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:17.160
purpose of gaining total control of their bodies!&nbsp;
Yes, you heard that right! Believe it or not,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:22.620
the same anomalous property which animates the&nbsp;
sugar golems’ treacle bodies is apparently capable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:28.560
of overriding the human nervous system&nbsp;
from inside. And that’s no joke, folks!

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.940
While these tasty treats might sound sweet&nbsp;
to eat, you’ll be a puppet of meat from your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.940 --> 00:07:39.900
head to feet if you don’t complete the tasks I&nbsp;
entreat. If an instance of SCP-3077-1 attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:44.940
to enter your mouth, you must remember first&nbsp;
and foremost to keep your trap shut - blocking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:50.160
it with a mask or similar article of clothing&nbsp;
if need be! Next, you must use your limbs and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:54.360
all available implements to batter the&nbsp;
attacking golem away while doing your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:58.920
best to keep a distance of at least arm’s&nbsp;
reach between yourself and the instance.

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:06.480
It should come as a relief to all rational people&nbsp;
that SCP-3077-1 instances are severely limited in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:12.000
their physical capabilities, and an adult human&nbsp;
of average fitness can easily hold one off if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:17.640
they know what to expect. The tricky part comes&nbsp;
from the amorphous properties of the instances’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:23.520
viscous treacle bodies, as well as their anomalous&nbsp;
ability to regenerate from any physical trauma.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:29.520
The only way to permanently destroy an&nbsp;
instance of SCP-3077-1 is to expose it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.600
to temperatures above its melting point&nbsp;
– which for you sticklers out there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:40.680
approximately 176 degrees celsius. The&nbsp;
most effective weapons against SCP-3077-1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:46.320
instances include fire bombs, flamethrowers,&nbsp;
and your run-of-the-mill convection ovens.

00:08:46.320 --> 00:08:51.780
If it is at all possible to contain the instance&nbsp;
within a sealed vessel such as a large Tupperware&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:57.480
or wooden barrel, then you oughta do whatever you&nbsp;
can to prevent the candy creeps from running amok.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:03.960
While ordinary below-zero temperatures are unable&nbsp;
to destroy the anomalous treacle of SCP-3077,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:11.880
instances of SCP-3077-1 can effectively be slowed&nbsp;
down or stopped completely if you put them on ice.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.640
Whether it's the hot foot or the cold shoulder,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:19.620
some form of extreme temperature should&nbsp;
always be weaponized when defending oneself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:27.300
from an SCP-3077-1 instance. Any attempt to&nbsp;
crush or smash an SCP-3077-1 instance will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:32.160
only result in the bad bonbon breaking apart&nbsp;
and reforming into several more belligerent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.160 --> 00:09:37.020
bite-sized blighters. A human under siege&nbsp;
by the sugar golems might find themselves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:41.160
quickly outnumbered if they foolishly attempt&nbsp;
to use a melee weapon against the anomalies.

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:46.440
Basically, it’s like a more delicious version&nbsp;
of the popular arcade video game Asteroids!

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:50.940
No? Ehh. I guess that reference&nbsp;
was from even before my time.

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:57.300
At any rate, instances of SCP-3077-1 are&nbsp;
difficult to destroy without access to heat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:02.460
or freezing. The tendency of the molasses&nbsp;
menaces to increase in number is made even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.460 --> 00:10:08.520
worse because of the fact that any amount of&nbsp;
SCP-3077 outside of containment can generate a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:16.920
nearly infinite number of SCP-3077-1. While even&nbsp;
an army of SCP-3077-1 instances is far weaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:22.260
than an equivalent pack of hunting animals, the&nbsp;
ability to continuously multiply and physiology&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.260 --> 00:10:26.880
that doesn’t experience the consequences&nbsp;
of fatigue means that given enough time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:33.060
the sugar golems can outlast any amount of human&nbsp;
resistance until they roll over their preferred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:39.960
prey like a slow insurmountable syrupy tsunami of&nbsp;
surrender. Seriously scary stuff, some would say.

00:10:39.960 --> 00:10:45.000
But what happens next is the real kicker,&nbsp;
folks! Mind this ballyhoo’s somber spiel!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:51.540
If an instance of SCP-3077-1 manages to, against&nbsp;
all odds, clamber its way into a human chatterbox&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:57.600
and hijack the poor sap’s nervous system, the&nbsp;
victim is immediately classified as SCP-3077-2.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.600 --> 00:11:06.180
SCP-3077-2 instances are easily distinguished from&nbsp;
unaffected humans on sight alone. Dark tendrils of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:11.820
SCP-3077 can be seen visibly moving beneath&nbsp;
the skin and often emerge from the mouth to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:11.820 --> 00:11:16.620
criss-cross the instance’s face like makeup,&nbsp;
the world’s most disturbing circus clown.

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:22.200
That’s not all! After the tragic treacly&nbsp;
transformation takes place, the movements&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:28.140
exhibited by the instance of SCP-3077-2 will&nbsp;
become crooked and jerky like a marionette&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:33.660
puppeteered by a frustrated chimpanzee! During&nbsp;
this time, the instance remains fully conscious,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:38.760
retaining whatever cognitive faculties it&nbsp;
had possessed previous to its classification,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:44.520
but it is unable to attempt speech or&nbsp;
exert autonomy over its own actions. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:50.760
fun fact was discovered by studying the EEG&nbsp;
recordings of several SCP-3077-2 instances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:55.140
and is brought to you by the United&nbsp;
Guild of the Existentially Terrified!

00:11:55.800 --> 00:12:01.620
If an instance of SCP-3077-2 happens to wander&nbsp;
its way into the vicinity of any humans that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:07.560
haven’t succumbed to the process of consuming&nbsp;
SCP-3077-1, it will proceed to put on a jaunty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:12.480
performance for its newfound audience. This&nbsp;
peculiar display involves clumsy efforts at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:17.820
dance choreography and the throaty singing of&nbsp;
unsettling atonal melodies that would make your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:22.620
annoying cousin’s road trip songs sound like&nbsp;
they’re in tune. These awkward performances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:28.320
continue until the audience departs from the&nbsp;
view of the SCP-3077-2 instance or the instance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:34.140
expires. This confirms that the point of the&nbsp;
gesture is to entertain, as without an audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:40.140
the SCP-3077-2 instance is not compelled&nbsp;
to make any noises of its own accord and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:43.500
in general, doesn’t do anything&nbsp;
other than move around aimlessly.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:51.240
In the event that any number SCP-3077-1 instances&nbsp;
escapes from containment and cause the creation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:57.660
SCP-3077-2, members of the mobile task force are&nbsp;
instructed to never stray from the line of sight&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:04.800
of a currently performing SCP-3077-2 instance&nbsp;
and to approach steadily before restraining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:10.740
the instance while causing minimal harm to&nbsp;
the body. SCP-3077-2 instances can be useful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:16.500
for running further tests on the anomalous&nbsp;
properties of SCP-3077, and there are simple&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.500 --> 00:13:21.840
procedures that allow an instance to be kept&nbsp;
alive indefinitely in containment. Any damage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:21.840 --> 00:13:26.760
sustained during capture can severely hamper the&nbsp;
efficiency of these life-sustaining procedures.

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:33.480
The worst-case scenario is that an SCP-3077-2&nbsp;
instance expires before being securely contained,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:39.720
as this will cause the SCP-3077-1 instance to&nbsp;
emerge from its host and resume its relentless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:47.820
attacks on all nearby humans. It is far easier to&nbsp;
simply deal with SCP-3077-2 instances accordingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.820 --> 00:13:54.180
and this is because SCP-3077-2 only ever&nbsp;
attempts to continue the performance and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:58.380
possesses neither the intention&nbsp;
nor the capacity for retaliation.

00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:02.880
If it is deemed necessary for the&nbsp;
effectiveness of a recapture effort,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:08.160
it can be permissible for the Mobile Task&nbsp;
Force to allow instances of SCP-3077-1&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:14.880
outside of containing to find purchase&nbsp;
within SCP-3077-2 to increase the ease&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:18.840
of containment and lessen the risk of&nbsp;
Foundation personnel being affected.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:23.880
The performances of SCP-3007-2&nbsp;
instances are rarely physically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:27.960
intensive enough to make capture too&nbsp;
difficult, but it can be said that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:27.960 --> 00:14:32.100
the whimsical antics of these affected&nbsp;
humans are anything but predictable!

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:38.520
During some rare and special performances,&nbsp;
and if the SCP-3077-1 instance in control&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:44.820
of the SCP-3077-2 instance is feeling&nbsp;
especially daring - it may try to show off an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:50.280
array of woefully inadequate acrobatic skills:&nbsp;
front flips that are more like belly flops,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:54.600
back flips that could be mistaken for&nbsp;
pratfalls, and the sort of tightrope and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:59.040
trapeze acts that are better left to the&nbsp;
imagination. In lieu of prior incidents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:05.160
The Foundation strongly advises that if&nbsp;
for any reason an instance of SCP-3077-2&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:10.080
must exist in containment, it must always be&nbsp;
prevented from being at an altitude of more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:15.300
than six feet from the surface of the floor.&nbsp;
Especially if any humans it would perceive as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:19.260
an audience are located directly beneath&nbsp;
where its performance would take place.

00:15:19.260 --> 00:15:26.100
Regarding the creation of further instances&nbsp;
of SCP-3077-2, requests from any level of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:31.440
Foundation personnel at Site-81 or elsewhere&nbsp;
must be granted permission to proceed by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:37.560
SCP-3077’s head researcher. Because of the&nbsp;
horrific implications of what happens to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.560 --> 00:15:44.340
the still-aware human mind while the body is&nbsp;
affected by SCP-3077-1, this process is only to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:44.340 --> 00:15:50.820
be approved for use on D-class personnel. That’s&nbsp;
right! And even then - in the event that all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.820 --> 00:15:55.320
rigamarole of the paperwork goes through,&nbsp;
it is not acceptable to create an instance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.320 --> 00:16:01.860
SCP-3077-2 merely for the purpose of providing&nbsp;
live entertainment to fellow researchers.

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:05.880
After all, not a single one of us should&nbsp;
be quick to forget the grotesque and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:11.340
highly regrettable spectacle that was Dr.&nbsp;
Deitz’ Deplorable D-Class Dancers. Every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:15.120
researcher involved with that ethical&nbsp;
nightmare was reprimanded severely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:20.040
and the colorful novelty costumes and jangling&nbsp;
bells that all former D-Class personnel were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:26.220
made to wear after being reclassified to&nbsp;
SCP-3077-2 have been permanently confiscated.

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:30.240
Let the cotton candy machine and&nbsp;
peanut dispenser located just outside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:36.120
the containment unit of SCP-3077 serve&nbsp;
as a stern reminder that there’s a time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:41.880
and place for monkeyshines and tomfoolery, and&nbsp;
sometimes - yes, every now and then - a highly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:46.380
secure Foundation facility is neither&nbsp;
the right place nor the right time.

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:52.740
In case you haven’t picked up on it, there are&nbsp;
very few practical applications of SCP-3077 due to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:58.020
the fact that its status as a food dish is negated&nbsp;
by the consequences of consumption. The main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.020 --> 00:17:04.980
reason for tests to be administered on SCP-3077-2&nbsp;
instances is to discover if there is a safe method&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:11.940
of extracting an SCP-3077-1 instance from the&nbsp;
body of its host without causing the expiration&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:17.040
of the original human. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
due to a persistent lack of success,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:17.040 --> 00:17:21.780
these experiments have been discontinued&nbsp;
indefinitely. But that just won’t do!

00:17:21.780 --> 00:17:26.340
How else are we supposed to know if these things&nbsp;
actually taste as good as they look? I won’t rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:31.440
until everyone is able to harmlessly ingest&nbsp;
a sugar golem of their very own! I might be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:37.320
old-fashioned, but to me, the safe object class&nbsp;
isn’t just a designation, it’s an invitation!

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:41.100
I oughta be completely okay doing&nbsp;
whatever I like around a safe object,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:46.620
because it’s safe! That word should actually&nbsp;
mean something - Ding dang darn it! And I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:50.520
don’t mean in the sense that the SCP&nbsp;
Foundation uses it, meaning an anomaly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:50.520 --> 00:17:54.420
that doesn’t present an active threat to&nbsp;
containment efforts! And more importantly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:54.420 --> 00:17:59.820
there aren’t that many anomalies that are also&nbsp;
delicious candy! And I want to eat this one!

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:03.960
Sorry, sorry, I lost my cool a bit&nbsp;
there… I just have such a sweet tooth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:08.220
and my brain is constantly drifting back to&nbsp;
my nostalgic childhood memories of playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:12.060
CandyLand with my family. That was before&nbsp;
they all decided that they wanted nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:15.840
to do with me because I became so obsessed&nbsp;
with dressing up like a carnival barker that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.840 --> 00:18:20.580
I drove away everyone who ever cared about&nbsp;
me. Other than that, my job here at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:20.580 --> 00:18:24.240
Foundation explaining confectionary SCPs&nbsp;
is the only thing I have left in my sad,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:29.820
sad life. Some days I feel less like Gloppy,&nbsp;
and more like a real Lord Licorice. In hard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:29.820 --> 00:18:33.900
times such as these, a fellow could really&nbsp;
use some entertainment to cheer himself up.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:39.480
Wait a flea-jumping moment! What is that? What’s&nbsp;
the big idea!? How did these escaped instances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:45.300
of SCP 3077-2 get in here? They’re all supposed&nbsp;
to be safe in containment a few floors down. Did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:48.840
somebody else from the research team let it in&nbsp;
here because they knew I was in costume standing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.840 --> 00:18:55.740
in front of a pretend fairground set? That’s in&nbsp;
pretty poor taste, don’t you think? Pun intended!

00:18:55.740 --> 00:19:00.660
I should probably report to the head researcher…&nbsp;
That would be the ethical, reasonable thing to do…

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:07.140
Then again… look at ‘em all go! Those sure are&nbsp;
some hilarious dances! I’m definitely seeing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:13.140
snappy attempt at doing the Charleston - a classic&nbsp;
- and is that one doing the worm or… it is just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:18.300
flopping on the floor? I think one of these&nbsp;
instances knows about that Fortnite stuff all the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:18.300 --> 00:19:23.400
kids are into these days, but I’m not sure if it’s&nbsp;
the human element or the golem that decides what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:29.640
dances it knows. Either way, this was actually&nbsp;
exactly what I needed to feel so much better!

00:19:29.640 --> 00:19:35.100
For once, it feels like I’m actually at a carnival&nbsp;
instead of just pretending to be at one! This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:35.100 --> 00:19:39.540
the greatest performance I’ve ever seen in&nbsp;
all years - which you can be sure that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:39.540 --> 00:19:40.589
have been a lot of! Until next time gents and&nbsp;
jolly strangers! I hope you enjoyed the show!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:40.589 --> 00:19:40.680
Just remember, the next time you’re hankering&nbsp;
for a snack - watch your back! Ha! Ha! Ha!

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:48.300
Now go check out “SCP-261 - Pan-Dimensional&nbsp;
Vending Machine” and “SCP-5962 - One Night&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:52.740
at McDonalds” for more anomalies&nbsp;
that’ll really whet your appetite!

